  "sources": [
    "Script: Wikipedia, \"Boro language (India)\", read 2026-11-22: written in Devanagari since 1975; the Bodo Sahitya Sabha accepted Devanagari in the April 1975 Memorandum of Understanding. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boro_language_(India)",
    "Letter inventory and order: Unicode CLDR common/main/brx.xml exemplar characters, index set (अ आ इ ई उ ऊ ऍ ए ऐ ऑ ओ औ क ख ग घ च छ ज झ ञ ट ठ ड ड़ ढ ण त थ द ध न प फ ब भ म य र ल ळ व श ष स ह), read 2026-11-22. https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr/blob/main/common/main/brx.xml",
    "CLDR is a locale data set, NOT the Bodo Sahitya Sabha alphabet. A Bodo teacher must confirm the inventory and order against the Sabha primer (e.g. whether ऍ ऑ ळ ड़ belong in a children's alphabet, and whether ङ ऋ are missing).",
    "Numerals १–२०: CLDR brx.xml lists the native numbering system as deva (Devanagari digits).",
    "Not included: vowel signs, number words, picture words (no cited source)."
  ]
